{"name":"Goddess","hex":"#d0e1e8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Goddess","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The single goddess of various monotheistic religions.","The single goddess of various bitheistic or duotheistic religions.\n The Lady, the main deity in Wicca."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Goddess"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goddess","blocks":[{"text":"A goddess is a female deity. In some faiths, a sacred female figure holds a central place in religious prayer and worship. For example, Shaktism, holds that the ultimate deity, the source of all reality, is Supreme Goddess (Mahamaya) and in some forms of Tantric Shaivism, the pair of Shiva and Shakti are the ultimate principle. Meanwhile, in Vajrayana Buddhism, ultimate reality is often seen as being composed of two principles depicted as two deities in union symbolising the non-duality of the two principles of perfect wisdom (female) and skillful compassion (male). A single figure in a monotheistic faith that is female may be identified simply as god because of no need to differentiate by gender or with a diminutive. An experiment to determine the effect of psychedelics on subjects composed of leaders from diverse religious groups revealed a general experience that the divine which the subjects encountered was feminine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Queen_Nefertari_being_led_by_Isis_MET_DP167142.jpg/330px-Queen_Nefertari_being_led_by_Isis_MET_DP167142.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goddess","wikidata":"Q205985"},{"title":"Goddess (Banks album)","blocks":[{"text":"Goddess is the debut studio album by American singer and songwriter Banks, released on September 5, 2014, by Harvest Records. The album includes songs from her previous extended plays Fall Over and London. The album spawned four singles: \"Warm Water\", \"Brain\", \"Drowning\", and \"Beggin for Thread\". A companion remix album, Goddess Remixes, was released digitally on March 23, 2015. To mark the album's tenth anniversary, Goddess: Unplugged featuring acoustic versions of 10 tracks from the standard album was released on December 13, 2024."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/BanksGoddessCover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goddess_(Banks_album)","wikidata":"Q16915466"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Ceres_statue.jpg/330px-Ceres_statue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Ceres_statue.jpg/330px-Ceres_statue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of an unknown woman as Ceres, Roman goddess of agriculture and motherly relationships","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeres_statue.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Freia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg/500px-Freia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Freia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg/500px-Freia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The goddess Freyja is nuzzled by the boar Hildisvíni while gesturing to Hyndla (1895) by Lorenz Frølich.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFreia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Toci_and_Xochiquetzal%2C_Two_Aztec_Goddesses_WDL6731.png/500px-Toci_and_Xochiquetzal%2C_Two_Aztec_Goddesses_WDL6731.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wi